	(text "2 Cell Li-po Battery\nWith thermistor taped on it\nassemble two 18650 single cell batteries \n(with least 3000mAh to 3500mAh capacity each)\nand add the mid point cable between the two"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 229.362 112.776 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
				(color 238 0 0 1)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2de54e07-c6c8-4d78-9aaf-d5eb30ea7f31")
	)
	(text "LTST-C170GKT\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 408.94 152.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.508 0.508)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3ad44e95-3bb4-4cac-b03e-8d59f96ab9ff")
	)
	(text "A standard USB-C receptacle has VBUS pins on both \nthe top row (A4, A9) and bottom row (B4, B9). \nThis ensures that no matter which way you flip the cable,\n the power pins always align. (Same for ground)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 157.988 23.876 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "65007e1c-24ab-4910-b050-7bd115ece8c4")
	)
	(text "break this pin out to a test point on your PCB. \nDuring your initial testing, you can use a multimeter \nto measure the voltage and calculate exactly how much \n\"fuel\" your robot is consuming without having to cut \nwires to insert an ammeter."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.478 169.164 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "660172e7-640f-4fa2-a631-46f73e372569")
	)
	(text "LTST-C170GKT\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 151.13 139.954 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.508 0.508)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6d0f9482-0c8c-4f0f-903e-280efd1d5f4c")
	)
	(text "LTST-C170GKT\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 391.16 137.668 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.508 0.508)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7e9260da-7cc0-48c6-a39c-a4a9f16c36cc")
	)
	(text "USB Inserted: The chip detects 5V on VL. ACOK pulls internal switch to Ground (LOW). \n-> MODE goes LOW \n-> Chip enters Charge Mode.\n\nUSB Removed: ACOK lets go (High Impedance). \n->The 10kΩ resistor pulls MODE up to VCC (HIGH). \n-> Chip enters Discharge Mode."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 141.732 153.416 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "96ec2f84-4415-4f2f-87e3-9d4ec1895d9e")
	)
	(text "USB Power Source: \nUse a high-quality 5V/3A (15W) wall adapter. \nIf we use a weak 1A phone charger, \nthe device will charge very slowly or the Pi might reboot."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 42.418 31.242 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 255 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9b5b1db8-5b59-41bc-a499-9070af8a0134")
	)
	(text "LTST-C170GKT\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 396.24 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.508 0.508)
			)
		)
		(uuid "aacec0d7-3e97-4485-8a95-ac85e48e0231")
	)
	(text "Charge Current - ISET - 143 kΩ = 1.5A\nInput Limit - ILIM - 71.5 kΩ = 3A Limit from USB (Safe for most adapters)\nDischarge Limit - OLIM - 43 kΩ = 4.9A Limit\nLogic Pull-up - ACOK - 10 kΩ (Standard Pull-up)\nTemp Fake (High),VNTC to NTC,10 kΩ,Part 1 of Voltage Divider\nTemp Fake (Low),NTC to AGND,10 kΩ,Part 2 of Voltage Divider"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 139.954 167.132 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "baa15373-9201-4bd8-9cc5-ae615f5e069d")
	)
